\n\nLet $\\mathcal{P} \\subset \\mathbb{R}^{n}$ be a polytope whose vertices have rational coordinates. By a seminal result of E. Ehrhart, the number of integer lattice points in the $k$th dilate of $\\mathcal{P}$ ($k$ a positive integer) is a quasi-polynomial function of $k$ — that is, a \"polynomial\" in which the coefficients are themselves periodic functions of $k$. It is an open problem to determine which quasi-polynomials are the Ehrhart quasi-polynomials of rational polytopes. As partial progress on this problem, we construct families of polytopes in which the periods of the coefficient functions take on various prescribed values.\n\n  * PDF\n\nPublished\n\n2018-03-16\n\nHow to Cite\n\nMcAllister, T. B., & Rochais, H. O. (2018). Periods of Ehrhart Coefficients of Rational Polytopes. The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 25(1), #P1.64. https://doi.org/10.37236/6059\n\nIssue\n\nVolume 25, Issue 1 (2018)\n\nArticle Number\n\nP1.64--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe minimum period of the Ehrhart quasi-polynomial of a rational polytope (https://research.tue.nl/en/publications/the-minimum-period-of-the-ehrhart-quasi-polynomial-of-a-rational-/)\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # The minimum period of the Ehrhart quasi-polynomial of a rational polytope ... McAllister ... The minimum period of the Ehrhart quasi-polynomial of a rational polytope.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Minimum Period of the Ehrhart Quasi-polynomial of a Rational Polytope - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/math/0310255v1)\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 23.1 years ago; Crawled: last month; ## The Minimum Period of the Ehrhart Quasi-polynomial of a Rational Polytope ... McAllister, Kevin M. ... If $P\\subset \\R^d$ is a rational polytope, then $i_P(n):=#(nP\\cap \\Z^d)$ is a quasi-polynomial 